Addresses inefficient regex compilation in the OpenAPI JSON preprocessing step where a pattern was being recompiled on every match.

**Changes:**
- Extract `number_regex` pattern compilation outside the `replace_all` closure
- Compile both regex patterns once at function scope for reuse

**Before:**
```rust
let fixed_content = regex::Regex::new(r#"("type"\s*:\s*"string"[^}]*?"enum"\s*:\s*\[)([^\]]+)(\])"#)
    .expect("...")
    .replace_all(&json_content, |caps: &regex::Captures| {
        // This regex is recompiled on every match ❌
        let fixed_enum = regex::Regex::new(r#"\b(\d+)\b"#)
            .expect("...")
            .replace_all(enum_content, r#""$1""#);
        // ...
    });
```

**After:**
```rust
let type_enum_regex = regex::Regex::new(r#"("type"\s*:\s*"string"[^}]*?"enum"\s*:\s*\[)([^\]]+)(\])"#)
    .expect("...");
let number_regex = regex::Regex::new(r#"\b(\d+)\b"#)
    .expect("...");

let fixed_content = type_enum_regex
    .replace_all(&json_content, |caps: &regex::Captures| {
        // Reuse compiled regex ✓
        let fixed_enum = number_regex.replace_all(enum_content, r#""$1""#);
        // ...
    });
```

