The editor panel contained ~180 lines of duplicate function definitions, and the UI was a single flat form. This PR removes the duplication and implements a modern tabbed interface with four tabs: SYSTEM, ROUTES, SECTORS, and META.

## Changes

**Code deduplication** (dm4-panels-editor.js)
- Removed 7 duplicate function definitions inside `EditorPanel` function (lines 964-1140)
- Moved `getCurrentDatasetId` to module level for shared access
- Reduced file from 1450 to 1270 lines

**Tabbed UI implementation**
- **SYSTEM tab**: Edit selected system (name, coords, sector, notes) or enable "Add System Mode" via checkbox
- **ROUTES tab**: Placeholder for route management
- **SECTORS tab**: List all sectors with system counts, create new sectors
- **META tab**: Edit dataset metadata (name, version, description) and view statistics

**Map integration** (dm4-map-layers.js)
- Click handler for `add_system` mode: prompts for system ID/sector at clicked coordinates
- Click handler for `move_system` mode: updates system position to clicked coordinates
- Cursor changes to crosshair when editor mode is active
- Fixed `isPanning` variable scoping issue

**Styling** (dm-style-palette-e2.css)
- Tab buttons with active states
- Form inputs (textbox, textarea, checkbox, select)
- Mode indicator and delete button styling

## Before/After

**Before:** Single flat form with duplicate code
```javascript
// Inside EditorPanel function - duplicates module-level definitions
function dm4ValidateDb5Structure(db5) { /* ... */ }
function dm4ApplyChangeSector(db5, job, strict) { /* ... */ }
function dm4ApplyEditorJobToDb5(db5, job, strict) { /* ... */ }
// ... 5 more duplicate functions
```

**After:** Clean tabbed interface using module-level functions
```javascript
// Tab switching
var activeTab = "system";
tabButtons[tabName].addEventListener("click", function () {
  activeTab = tabName;
  render(state.getState());
});

// Render appropriate tab content
if (activeTab === "system") {
  renderSystemTab(tabContent, st, systems, selId, sectorList, jobs);
} else if (activeTab === "routes") {
  renderRoutesTab(tabContent, st, systems, hyperlanes, jobs);
}
```

